318-### 3.1 Guide chapter-family quick lookup
319-
320-When Codex is maintaining reflection against a governing guide, use these anchor routes:
321-
322:- Prompt Chaining / Planning -> base prompts; keep staged dependency, checkpoint, and fallback visibility explicit instead of collapsing into one-shot execution language
323-- Routing / Prioritization / Exploration -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo` or `Prioritization queue / next-action memo`
324-- Parallelization / Multi-Agent / A2A -> `PROMPT_multi_agent_overlay` + `orchestration-control`; prefer `Delegation admission memo`, `A2A task-handoff memo`, and `Join-quality review memo`
325-- Tool Use / MCP -> `PROMPT_tool_protocol_overlay`; prefer `Tool capability contract / precondition memo` or `MCP capability handoff memo`
326-- Memory / Learning / Adaptation -> `PROMPT_memory_adaptation_overlay`; prefer `Memory scope / checkpoint profile memo`, `Learning-signal review memo`, and `Adaptation decision memo`
327-- Goal / Monitoring / Recovery / HITL -> base prompts; prefer `Goal-monitoring status memo`, `Recovery / escalation checkpoint memo`, and `HITL approval packet`
328-- Retrieval / RAG -> `PROMPT_retrieval_grounding_overlay` + `grounded-research`; prefer `Evidence target / retrieval-mode memo` or `Source consultation ledger`
329-- Resource-Aware Optimization -> base prompts plus `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo`
330-- Reasoning Techniques / Reflection -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Critique quality review memo` when critique utility or no-gain loops are under review
331:- Appendix A / advanced prompting execution families -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay` for decomposition, step-back, self-consistency, ReAct-like loops, tree-style search, and bounded reflection; keep prompt chaining in base prompts and treat example-catalog references as structure-only
332-- Guardrails / Safety -> `PROMPT_guardrails_safety_overlay`
333:- Evaluation / Monitoring -> `PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay` + `eval-ops`; prefer `Benchmark registry memo`, `Guide reflection benchmark memo`, or `Prompt-stack release review`
334-
335-Lookup rule:
336-- if a chapter family can only be answered by operator-facing prose and not by the active runtime / skill surface, treat that as a reflection gap and patch the actual prompt docs before claiming parity
337-
338-Packet rule:
339-- one packet should solve one control problem
340-- if packet overhead exceeds its decision value, simplify or drop it
341-- if a task family has a required packet floor, do not silently downgrade it to an optional convenience note
342-- `PROMPT_guideline` direct packet floor matrix owns first-pass `required / recommended / optional packet` decisions; `Packet compliance report` audits observed-vs-required coverage, omission findings, and claim downgrades against that floor
343-- if the required packet exists but the recommended companion is missing, keep the narrower companion-missing language rather than full-strength claim language
344-- if future behavior or reusable defaults are being changed, pair `Learning-signal review memo` with `Adaptation decision memo` rather than silently mutating defaults
345-- if async or delegated work remains active, prefer lifecycle packets over prose-only status narration
346-- host-runtime maintenance and release reviews should still be able to see whether packet families cover the active control boundaries
347-- keep guide / runtime / skill lookup parity visible for goal, recovery, approval, budget, prioritization, readiness, and lifecycle-audit packets; do not let one layer silently know a family the others no longer expose
348:- keep coding-briefing, research-transparency, resource-concurrency, packet-compliance, replay-review, release-evidence, benchmark-registry, context-sufficiency, critique-quality, adaptation-promotion, and route-quality packets equally visible when those are the live control boundaries
349:- keep benchmark-execution, replay-verdict, context-failure, critique-utility, adaptation-lifecycle, route-reprioritization, coding-proof, release-v2, and telemetry-trend packets equally visible when those are the live control boundaries
350-- packet presence is not operational proof; if execution, controller behavior, or promotion evidence is the live question, choose the artifact that actually carries the linked evidence
351-- distinguish `light review memo`, `stronger packet`, and `operational artifact` rather than treating every packet as equal-strength evidence
352-- if a lighter memo and a stronger artifact address the same control problem, keep the stronger artifact active and background or supersede the lighter memo
353-- if the task has crossed from packet presence review into operational proof review, prefer the stronger operational artifact and mark weaker packets as superseded rather than silently doubling them
354-- if two compatible artifacts share one lineage, let the newer artifact supersede the stale predecessor explicitly
355:- treat `Benchmark cohort manifest`, `Replay runner verdict sheet`, `Adaptation controller audit packet`, `Coding benchmark execution ledger`, `Release promotion decision record`, `Telemetry drift investigation memo`, `Route-switch benchmark verdict`, and `Context substrate scorecard` as the direct packet floor before benchmark-grade, replay-grade, controller-grade, coding-proof-grade, release-grade, drift-grade, route-quality-grade, or retrieval-substrate-grade language
356:- keep shared identifiers such as `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` stable whenever benchmark, replay, adaptation, release, or telemetry packets must be linked across rounds
357-- when artifacts are joined, check precedence, compatibility, freshness, and completeness first; reject incompatible merges and preserve upstream source IDs and `artifact_version` in the surviving artifact
358-- keep failure classes such as `false-promotion`, `false-hold`, `drift-triggered review`, `rollback aftermath`, `route-switch failure`, `late clarification`, and `failed fallback timing` independently diagnosable when those control surfaces are active
359-- keep `runner readiness failure`, `partial completion`, `quarantine entry`, `freshness defect`, and `unresolved join failure` independently visible when they drive escalation, downgrade, split verdict retention, or join rejection
360-- if critique benefit itself must be proven rather than praised, escalate from critique review prose or `Critique utility scorecard` to `Critique delta ledger`
