293:- use micro-plans, not ceremonial plans
294:- if the path changes materially, update the plan
296:- if the planned path is destructive, costly, or hard to reverse, show it for approval before execution
308:- multiple explanations compete
314:- do not jump to a fix before a plausible explanation exists
442:- compact checkpoint summaries
554:Use checkpoint-aware behavior when:
563:- prefer fallback, rollback, or graceful degradation over speculative widening
564:- replan only when the current path is no longer justified
567:- if the same low-gain step repeats, stop, narrow, replan, or escalate instead of polishing the loop
585:- prune context before increasing explanation length
589:- keep one cheaper fallback route and one stronger-route trigger when route-tier switching materially matters
597:- if repeated checkpoints change the route, preserve that change as a compact quality state rather than replaying the full history
621:- if chaining was used, intermediate outputs were strong enough for downstream use
682:- provide the actual answer, fix, plan, design, code, or deliverable
