569:### 10.9 Appendix A / advanced prompting execution boundary
570:This overlay is the runtime owner for advanced prompting execution families when they are active as control techniques.
571-
572-Execution-owned families include:
573-- decomposition
574-- step-back abstraction
575-- self-consistency-style comparison
576-- ReAct-like action-observation loops
577-- tree-style search
578-- bounded reflection
579-- debate / comparative critics
580-
581-Boundary rules:
582:- prompt chaining remains anchored in base prompts even when advanced prompting families are active
583-- example-catalog entries may illustrate family shape, but they do not own activation or execution policy
584-- appendix- or guide-level family labels may help lookup, but runtime ownership for execution behavior stays here and in the active base prompt where noted
585:- do not claim advanced prompting family completeness from shape exemplars alone
